### Task 12: cue2openapi upstream-migration fidelity changes
#
# cue2openapi now generates from cuelang.org/go/encoding/openapi rather than a
# hand-rolled AST walk. Embedded CUE definitions are emitted as
# `allOf` against the embedded schema instead of being dropped, and 51
# properties plus 21 required constraints that the previous generator
# silently omitted are now present. No property or constraint that CUE actually
# enforces was removed; the change is structural, so oasdiff reports it against
# the v1 baseline. Two removals are deliberate fixes oasdiff did not flag: the
# old walker leaked the hidden CUE uniqueness-check fields `_uniqueTermIds`
# (Lexicon) and `_uniqueMappingIds` (MappingDocument) into the published schema
# as REQUIRED properties, so documents had to carry internal bookkeeping to
# validate.
#
# Non-empty-tuple fields (CUE `[T, ...T]`) now surface their CUE-enforced
# minimum length as `minItems: 1`, which the old walker did not emit.
request-property-min-items-increased AssessmentLog
request-property-min-items-increased AssessmentRequirement
request-property-min-items-increased Catalog
request-property-min-items-increased Control
request-property-min-items-increased ControlEvaluation
request-property-min-items-increased RACI
request-property-min-items-increased Threat

# CUE regex constraints (`=~"..."`) on these fields now surface as an
# OpenAPI `pattern`, which the old walker did not emit.
request-property-pattern-added Entity
request-property-pattern-added EvidenceMapping
request-property-pattern-added MappingReference

# Two distinct fidelity fixes fold into this (id, schema) pair:
#   - AssessmentLog.steps-executed is `int` in CUE (evaluationlog.cue); the old
#     walker mistranslated it as `string`.
#   - Evidence.payload is CUE's top type `_` (auditlog.cue:92), so it accepts
#     any value; the old walker emitted `string`, forcing structured inline
#     evidence to be serialised.
request-property-type-changed AssessmentLog
response-property-type-changed AssessmentLog

# Datetime is `time.Format("2006-01-02T15:04:05Z07:00")` (a full RFC 3339
# datetime) in CUE; the old walker mistranslated it as OpenAPI format `date`.
response-body-type-changed Datetime

# The referenced schema's own `required` list is unchanged; oasdiff reports
# these nested paths as removed only because the field's `$ref` is now
# wrapped in `allOf` (to carry the field's own description) instead of being
# a bare `$ref` sibling.
