response-required-property-removed AssessmentRequirement
response-required-property-removed Catalog
response-required-property-removed Control
response-required-property-removed Log
response-required-property-removed Metadata
response-required-property-removed Threat

# `state` is `#Lifecycle: *"Active" | …` — it has a CUE default, so a producer
# may omit it and the consumer applies "Active". The old asset emitted it as
# required, which rejected documents the CUE accepts (the repo's own
# good-ccc.yaml, good-osps.yml and good-lifecycle.yaml among them). The
# projection now drops a defaulted field from `required` and publishes its
# `default` instead; oasdiff sees only the first half and calls it breaking.
# The same change on Recommendation and AcceptedMethod (`required: *false |
# bool`) is not listed because both schemas are experimental and already exempt.
